Step to reproduce,
1. create one index using below mappings
```
{
  "farequote-rt" : {
    "mappings" : {
      "dynamic" : "false",
      "runtime" : {
        "lowercase_airline" : {
          "type" : "keyword",
          "script" : {
            "source" : "emit(params._source.airline.toLowerCase())",
            "lang" : "painless"
          }
        },
        "responsetime" : {
          "type" : "double",
          "script" : {
            "source" : "emit(params._source.responsetime)",
            "lang" : "painless"
          }
        },
        "responsetime_bigger" : {
          "type" : "double",
          "script" : {
            "source" : "emit(params._source.responsetime * 2)",
            "lang" : "painless"
          }
        }
      },
      "properties" : {
        "@timestamp" : {
          "type" : "date"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

2. reindex `farequote` dataset to `farequote-rt`
3. create a regression job by using the below job configure:
```
{
  "id": "fq_rt_outliers",
  "create_time": 1606909980318,
  "version": "8.0.0",
  "description": "",
  "source": {
    "index": [
      "farequote-rt"
    ],
    "query": {
      "match_all": {}
    }
  },
  "dest": {
    "index": "fq_rt_outliers",
    "results_field": "ml"
  },
  "analysis": {
    "outlier_detection": {
      "compute_feature_influence": true,
      "outlier_fraction": 0.05,
      "standardization_enabled": true
    }
  },
  "analyzed_fields": {
    "includes": [
      "responsetime",
      "responsetime_bigger"
    ],
    "excludes": []
  },
  "model_memory_limit": "33mb",
  "allow_lazy_start": false,
  "max_num_threads": 1
}
```
3. run job,
4. job failed with this error on UI:
`No field [runtimefield] could be detected` 

regression job on `responsetime_bigger` as dependency_variable also fails with the same error, but was successfully to run if using `responsetime`.

